          "source_text_sha256": "2c66983ebc634912661aedb79d304e44a225bc42e8a37727876ad29231734b68",
          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On the night of May 14, 2008, between 9:30 PM and 10:30 PM, during a birthday party, three individuals observed the slow movement in an east-west direction of three glowing orbs of yellow-orange light. No sound was heard. The observation lasted less than a minute. Only one statement was collected. The witness's observation is characteristic of an observation of a release of Thai lanterns, both in terms of colors, shapes, and the type of trajectory. The general east-west direction of the movement is consistent with the direction of the wind measured in Avignon at 10:00 PM (easterly wind). Consequently, the GEIPAN classifies the case as B: probable observation of Thai lanterns.",
